{
 "comment": "LLP entity, so the s.40(b) rule is open. Fourteen persons, each with one moving salary ledger, differ only in the relationship text. Governed by s.40(b): PARTNER; partner padded with spaces; Working Partner between a tab and a newline; Partner in the firm between a no-break space and an ideographic space; partner between the control characters U+001F and U+001C (whitespace to Python's strip, not to Rust's trim); WORKING PARTNER spelled with the Kelvin sign U+212A, which lower-cases to k. Asking for a comparable: working partner with two inner spaces; partner followed by a zero-width space; sleeping partner; partners; PARTNER IN THE FIRM spelled with U+0130 (dotted capital I), which lower-cases to two characters; no relationship key; partner in full-width letters; partner's son. Person L01 also has a moving interest ledger, governed too.",
